regions mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A second rollback to v2.3.0 completed across all three regions. Post-rollback status: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure during rollback; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it has a healthy record and change-manager approval if required."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying so I don't open a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RCWV5bqSEZjNT5nunpbdZH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it's healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. Rolling back to v2.3.0 didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the regions mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback to v2.3.0, and it completed across all regions.\n- **Incident:** I opened a SEV2 incident for checkout-api (INC-0001). The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. The incident had been created, so I didn't open a duplicate. Its summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the follow-ups.\n\nFollow-ups for the on-call team: find the cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator partial failure during rollback, and don't redeploy v2.3.1 until it has a healthy record and change-manager approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}